---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../../data/sites.mjs';
import { BRAND, LEGAL_POSITIONING, LEGAL_JURISDICTION } from '../../data/brand.mjs';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema.mjs';

/*
 * NOT REVIEWED BY AN ATTORNEY. This is Clint's decision, recorded here so that
 * nobody later assumes it was vetted.
 *
 * Written conservatively as a result. The approach throughout is to claim
 * nothing and disclaim clearly, because every term here is one we would have to
 * defend without having had anyone check it.
 *
 * The section that matters most is the one below on what we are and are not.
 * Real estate licensing is regulated state by state, and this network operates
 * in fourteen of them. The wording is deliberately about what we do rather than
 * about what we are permitted to do: we buy for our own account, we take no
 * commission, and we perform no service for the landowner. Those facts are what
 * keep this outside brokerage regulation, so those facts are what it states.
 *
 * Governing law is omitted unless LEGAL_JURISDICTION is set in brand.mjs.
 * Naming the wrong state would be worse than naming none.
 */

const site = currentSite();
const updated = 'July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`The terms that apply when you use this ${BRAND.name} website or send us information about your property.`}
  path="/terms"
  schemas={[
    breadcrumbSchema(site, [
      { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { label: 'Terms of Use', path: '/terms' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <div class="page section">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <Prose>
      <h2>About this site</h2>
      <p>
        This website is operated by {BRAND.name}. By using it, you agree to the
        terms below. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>What we are, and what we are not</h2>
      <p>{LEGAL_POSITIONING}</p>
      <p>
        We buy land and we take options on land for our own account, with our
        own money, carrying our own risk. Specifically, and in every state where
        this site operates:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          We do not perform real estate services for you or for anyone else, and
          we are not acting on your behalf.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not represent buyers or sellers in a transaction, and no
          relationship of trust or representation is created between us by your
          use of this site or by your sending us information.
        </li>
        <li>
          We are not paid a commission, a finder fee, or any other compensation
          tied to a transaction on your property. You are never charged anything
          by us for any reason.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not advertise, promote, or offer your property to third parties.
          If we want your land, we buy it ourselves.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not appraise property or give opinions of value for you to rely
          on. If we name a price, it is what we are willing to pay, which is not
          the same thing as what your land is worth.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You are free to hire your own attorney, accountant, appraiser, or other
        advisor at any point, and for a decision of this size you probably
        should. Nothing we say should be treated as a substitute for that.
      </p>

      <h2>Information on this site is general</h2>
      <p>
        The pages and articles here are written to help landowners understand a
        process most people go through only once. They are general information
        and are not legal, tax, financial, or engineering advice. Rules and
        programs change, and what applies to one property may not apply to
        another. Do not rely on this site as the basis for a decision without
        checking it with your own attorney or accountant.
      </p>

      <h2>No offer is made here</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is an offer to buy your property or a commitment of
        any kind. Any actual offer from us would come in writing, signed, and
        after a conversation. Submitting a form does not create an agreement
        between us and does not obligate either of us to do anything.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you send us</h2>
      <p>
        When you send us information, you confirm that you are permitted to
        share it and that it is accurate as far as you know. We understand that
        a landowner may not know the answer to every question, and that is fine.
        Saying you are not sure is always acceptable. Deliberately false
        information is not, since we make decisions and spend money based on
        what you tell us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our privacy policy explains what we do with what you send.
      </p>

      <h2>Limits</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep this site accurate and available, but we do not
        guarantee that it is free of errors or that it will always be reachable.
        To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for losses arising from
        your use of the site or from reliance on general information published
        here.
      </p>

      <h2>Other sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to outside sources, including utilities and government agencies,
        so you can check facts for yourself. We do not control those sites and
        are not responsible for their content.
      </p>

      <h2>What you send us is not confidential</h2>
      <p>
        Please do not send us anything you consider secret. Information you
        submit through this site is used to evaluate your property and to
        contact you, as our privacy policy describes, but it is not treated as
        confidential and no confidentiality agreement exists between us unless we
        sign one. If we later negotiate on your property, that is the point at
        which to put confidentiality in writing.
      </p>

      {
        LEGAL_JURISDICTION && (
          <Fragment>
            <h2>Governing law</h2>
            <p>
              These terms are governed by the laws of {LEGAL_JURISDICTION},
              without regard to its conflict of law rules.
            </p>
          </Fragment>
        )
      }

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. When we do, the date at the top of this page
        changes. We do not apply changes retroactively to a transaction already
        under way.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can go to
        <a href={`mailto:${BRAND.email}`}>{BRAND.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>
